//! task: write
//! ask: Declare a module-level constant and use it to clamp a value.
//! expect: ok
//! refs: §4.1 rule 7, §8.6 decision 5
//! explain: A module-level `firma` is a constant. The initializer must be a plain literal today (an array literal at module level type-checks but does not lower, a documented implementation gap). Module-level `mutabilis` is not allowed: that is `EXS-E0500`.

firma LIMES: u64 = 3;

publica functio clausum(x: u64) -> u64 {
    si x gt LIMES { redde LIMES; }
    redde x;
}
